: \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f2143915e2c57d29d79f352f3c979678218c80af4d30b4093c78ae7bbccb535d","event_uuid":"989e75b1-4f91-440e-a811-c4f339df9e3e","position":{"commit_sha":"63e37cfb87f3fe7ccad531f879e8e2d71c14f891","position":"1786612638050128001-989e75b1-4f91-440e-a811-c4f339df9e3e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0c6ddc5a00108cd42e8a645ea38fa2ec6723b1a065021c8f2dc29aa5f73fe3f2","event_uuid":"4b3f93a5-d5c2-4991-832d-785e41bce466","position":{"commit_sha":"857e54946b885d90a772e9e5db0ca69a95e88347","position":"1786612646355414001-4b3f93a5-d5c2-4991-832d-785e41bce466"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"48aa715d57c66aa9bea7b0ab13bac56c3c62677ff138b2b482ab42d004e22751","event_uuid":"bcf36f89-326a-4485-a257-68c84e8c2153","position":{"commit_sha":"39549f6299caba74568c23396e0fbc79defa9abf","position":"1786638501427978001-bcf36f89-326a-4485-a257-68c84e8c2153"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Premise VALIDATED by reading current main; a second layer of repetition found that the ticket title does not name.\n\nLayer 1 (as filed): four guards each call `_run_request_sites()` — `test_the_provenance_analysis_can_see_the_sites_it_judges` (tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py:487), `test_no_run_request_inherits_the_raw_config_model` (495), `test_every_unfollowable_site_is_registered_with_a_reason\" (515), `test_neither_registry_has_stale_entries` (524). Each call re-walks `_SRC.rglob('*.py')` and re-parses every file mentioning `RunRequest(`.\n\nLayer 2 (not in the ticket): the cost of ONE call is itself dominated by repeated parsing. `_verdict`'s parameter-provenance branch (lines 448-450) re-walks `sorted(_SRC.rglob('*.py'))` and calls `ast.parse(caller_path.read_text())` on EVERY file in the tree, once per site whose config comes in as a parameter. `_functions()` (line 355) parses the whole tree again. That is why the ticket's own profile recorded ~8,033 parses for a single scan of a tree with far fewer files, and 32,124 for four scans.\n\nSo caching `_run_request_sites` per process (the filed fix) removes layer 1; memoising the per-path parse removes layer 2, which the four tests were each paying in full. The plan covers both, and the plan-review gate passed it with no blocking findings.\n\nSafety of caching: the analysis is a pure function of the committed `src/rebar` source. No test in the module mutates that tree, and the module's only autouse fixture (`class_table`, line 60) patches `llm_config._read_llm_file_table`, which the AST scan never consults.","timestamp":1786605140133374001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fix + measurements (local, quiet machine, `-p no:randomly`, whole module).\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| module wall | 50.14s | **5.96s** (-88%) |\n| module CPU (user+sys) | 46.13s | **6.24s** (-86%) |\n| the four guards | 11.87 + 11.85 + 11.83 + 10.90 = **46.45s** | one 4.14s fill + ~0.02s each |\n\n`_run_request_sites` invocation count, measured with a temporary pytest plugin that wraps the function and reports at session finish: **1** (was 4). AC met exactly.\n\nThe two layers separate cleanly in the numbers. Layer 1 (the filed concern, four repeats) accounts for the 4 -> 1 drop. Layer 2 (the per-path parse memo) shows up in the size of a SINGLE scan: 11.83s per call before, 4.14s after — **-65% on one scan**, because `_verdict` no longer re-reads and re-parses the whole tree once per parameter-provenance site and `_functions` no longer parses it again.\n\nEquivalence proven, not assumed. The origin/main version of the module and the changed version were both loaded in place and their `_run_request_sites()` output dumped to JSON:\n\n    sites before: 24  after: 24\n    IDENTICAL (order + content): True\n\nSo all 24 `(key, expr, verdict)` tuples are unchanged in value AND order; no assertion body or offender message was edited, only the parameter each test receives.\n\nDefect seeding: a `_seeded_defect_probe` was added to `src/rebar/llm/enrich.py` building `RunRequest(config=cfg, ...)` from `LLMConfig.from_env()`. Through the cached path the guard still catches it by name:\n\n    E   AssertionError: these RunRequest sites inherit cfg.model instead of selecting a model class (bug afeb): {'llm/enrich.py::_seeded_defect_probe': 'cfg'}\n    FAILED tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py::test_no_run_request_inherits_the_raw_config_model\n\nReverted immediately; `git status` shows only the test file modified.\n\nCross-session staleness: nothing is written to disk. The cache is a pytest session fixture plus a `functools.cache` on `_parsed`, both of which die with the process, so a later session cannot be served a pre-change analysis. `src/rebar` is read-only to this suite, and the module's only autouse fixture patches `llm_config._read_llm_file_table`, which the AST scan never consults.\n\nGates: 11 `check_*` pass, complexity `new=0 increased=0 stale=0`, lint and typecheck clean.","timestamp":1786608601859062001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Full-suite run for this change: **12677 passed, 52 skipped, 1 failed** in 1061s.\n\nThe single failure is NOT caused by this change and is filed separately as `future-fibroid-hammerkop` (9151-907b-471d-4a38), linked `discovered_from` the same audit parent:\n\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py::test_pass_summary_reports_the_decline_count`\n\nGrounds for attributing it elsewhere:\n- this change touches ONLY `tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py`, and adds no import-time side effect and no cross-module state — a session fixture and a `functools.cache`, both confined to that module's namespace;\n- the failing test predates all four tickets in this batch (`4010da6493`, 'Decline removals of never-confirmed peer links') and is an ancestor of the base this batch branched from;\n- it PASSED in the two earlier full-suite runs of this same batch;\n- it passes in isolation (10 passed) and passes `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` under `-n 3 --dist worksteal` three consecutive times (2575 passed each).\n\nMechanism identified while triaging: the summary line the test asserts is emitted under `if declined:` in `apply_inbound_records.py`, and `declined` only increments when `confirm_store is not None`. With no confirm store the removal is still declined and still logged PER ITEM — which is exactly the message caplog held — but the summary never fires. So the ordering-sensitive input is `confirm_store` resolution. Details and acceptance criteria are on the new ticket.","timestamp":1786610532833068001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"OSS consensus audit (2026-08-13): APPROVED pattern, already merged as 012854fb86.\n\nPylint constructs an immutable Astroid Project once in a module-scoped fixture and reuses it across diagram-analysis tests (pylint-dev/pylint@03eaf44, tests/pyreverse/test_diadefs.py#L59-L68). Astroid uses session fixtures for stable source corpora in its end-to-end benchmarks (pylint-dev/astroid@04ba439, tests/benchmarks/test_bench_endtoend.py#L103-L114).\n\nThe merged session fixture plus per-path parse memoization is the same lifecycle: immutable analysis state is shared only inside one pytest process/session, while every guard and defect-seeded assertion remains. Tracker cross-check found no rejection or competing ownership.","timestamp":1786638501427978001}],"created_at":1786598869895791001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2bfb528f-b152-4550-8878-7399361ebaa2","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ba7d-a412-bbc0-45cb"},{"link_uuid":"ed658c1a-db3e-4a1b-baba-e3f37b9f369a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7626-dfce-0157-474d"},{"link_uuid":"4b3f93a5-d5c2-4991-832d-785e41bce466","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"afeb-bc04-3265-4747"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nFour guards in `tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py` each call\n`_run_request_sites()` (line 467), which re-derives the SAME immutable analysis of\nthe whole `src/rebar` tree: `test_the_provenance_analysis_can_see_the_sites_it_judges`\n(line 487), `test_no_run_request_inherits_the_raw_config_model` (line 495),\n`test_every_unfollowable_site_is_registered_with_a_reason` (line 515) and\n`test_neither_registry_has_stale_entries` (line 524). CI recorded 30.10s, 32.27s,\n31.02s and 32.50s for them in one contended run.\n\nThe analysis is expensive twice over, and the second reason is not in the ticket\ntitle. `_run_request_sites` walks `_SRC.rglob(\"*.py\")` and parses every file that\nmentions `RunRequest(`. For each site it calls `_verdict`, whose parameter-provenance\nbranch (lines 448-450) re-walks `sorted(_SRC.rglob(\"*.py\"))` and calls\n`ast.parse(caller_path.read_text())` on EVERY file in the tree, once per site it has\nto follow — which is why a single scan was profiled at ~8,033 parses over a tree\nwith far fewer files. So the repetition is both across the four tests and inside\neach one.\n\nThe analysis is a pure function of the committed source: no test mutates\n`src/rebar`, and the module's only autouse fixture (`class_table`, line 60) patches\n`llm_config._read_llm_file_table`, which the AST scan never consults.\n\n## Approach\n\nCompute the analysis once per test process, and stop the inner scan re-reading the\ntree.\n\n* Add a session-scoped fixture `run_request_sites` that calls `_run_request_sites()`\n  once and returns its list; the four guards take it as a parameter instead of\n  calling the function. A pytest fixture is bounded by the session that created it,\n  so the cached value cannot outlive the run or be served to a later session — the\n  staleness requirement is satisfied by construction rather than by an\n  invalidation rule that could itself be wrong. `_run_request_sites` stays a plain\n  function so the fixture, and any future caller, can still invoke it directly.\n* Memoise the per-path parse behind a module-level\n  `_parsed(path) -> ast.Module` keyed on the path, used by `_run_request_sites`,\n  `_functions` (line 355) and `_verdict`'s caller scan (line 450). Within one\n  process each file is then read and parsed at most once, which removes the inner\n  repetition the four tests were each paying in full.\n\nBoth halves are caching only: the same `(key, expr, verdict)` tuples are produced,\nin the same order, and every assertion, offender message and registry check is\nuntouched. Deriving the analysis once is the smallest change that removes the\nrepetition without weakening what the guards inspect — the alternative of narrowing\nthe scan (fewer files, cheaper heuristics) would trade coverage for time, and these\nguards exist precisely because a vacuous scan is the failure mode\n(`test_the_provenance_analysis_can_see_the_sites_it_judges` guards the guard).\n\n## Scope\n\n* `tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py` — add `_parsed`, route the three\n  parse sites through it, add the session-scoped `run_request_sites` fixture, and\n  change the four guards to take it.\n\nNo production change: `src/rebar` is READ by the scan and not modified.\n\n## Testing\n\n* Happy path — all four guards still pass and still see the real tree:\n  `test_the_provenance_analysis_can_see_the_sites_it_judges` continues to assert\n  `>= 15` sites with a non-empty `config=` on each, which is what makes the other\n  three non-vacuous.\n* Equivalence check — the analysis produced through the fixture and the parse memo\n  is compared element-by-element against the result of the pre-change code on the\n  same tree, and must be identical.\n* Failure/edge path — a defect is seeded by adding a `RunRequest(config=cfg, ...)`\n  site to a real `src/rebar` module and confirming\n  `test_no_run_request_inherits_the_raw_config_model` FAILS naming that site\n  through the cached path. Seed reverted, not committed.\n* Whole-suite regression — the CI pytest command is green.\n\nNo wall-clock or timing-budget assertion is added; savings go in ticket comments.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `_run_request_sites` is invoked exactly once per test process when the four\n      guards run, verified by counting invocations with a temporary wrapper during\n      a focused run and reporting the count in a ticket comment.\n- [x] The four guards' assertions, offender messages and both registry checks are\n      unchanged in meaning — verified by `git diff` showing no edit to any assert\n      body or message, only the parameter each test receives.\n- [x] The list of `(key, expr, verdict)` tuples is byte-identical before and after\n      the change, verified by capturing it on `origin/main` and on the change and\n      comparing.\n- [x] A seeded raw-config `RunRequest` site is still caught by\n      `test_no_run_request_inherits_the_raw_config_model`, with the offender key in\n      the failure message — evidence in a ticket comment, seed reverted.\n- [x] The cache is a pytest session fixture plus a process-local parse memo, with\n      no on-disk artifact, so nothing survives the pytest session — verified by\n      `git diff` showing no file is written.\n- [x] Before/after durations for the four guards are measured with\n      `pytest --durations` and posted as a ticket comment.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py","reason":"derive the RunRequest provenance analysis once per process via a session fixture and memoise the per-path AST parse the inner caller scan repeats"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","7626-dfce-0157-474d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"ccb5ba3a-9066-4681-87c5-b555a1b5719d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["ci","performance","tests","llm"],"ticket_id":"fa90-3292-38d4-4fd2","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Four model-provenance guards repeat the same whole-tree AST analysis","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f2807268-70fd-4ada-945d-d3763c3f5321","2bfb528f-b152-4550-8878-7399361ebaa2","f30315b3-06c1-4f29-9104-fcf8ecc38e11","2f4a1b45-0a14-447a-9e2a-9b3105c35968","4461c525-2563-4ccb-a8aa-dbec430b21d2","38d8e29d-a9fb-4294-886a-de5a26de1524","25cacd11-5e16-409c-b6d1-89838064a284","7ec1990b-ab9f-4f79-bae9-8e625fd8a326","84733f15-2e87-424a-895e-e7df2fba04b3","ed658c1a-db3e-4a1b-baba-e3f37b9f369a","6df0987a-a641-437c-9efe-bdf0ecf587f4","218bd180-4290-4f6d-a257-85e168c8c980","ccb5ba3a-9066-4681-87c5-b555a1b5719d","989e75b1-4f91-440e-a811-c4f339df9e3e","4b3f93a5-d5c2-4991-832d-785e41bce466","bcf36f89-326a-4485-a257-68c84e8c2153"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659698078962001,"uuid":"dc3a9be7-dbec-46d5-bd85-358c6bbe13db"}